<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
<p class="font-bold">Move the number 5 from the high group to the low group.</p>
<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-base">
<div class="border-2 border-ink p-3"><strong>Before</strong><p>R: 1, 2, 3, 4</p><p>Average 2.5</p><p class="mt-2">S: <strong>5</strong>, 6, 7, 8, 9</p><p>Average 7</p></div>
<div class="border-2 border-ink p-3"><strong>After</strong><p>R: 1, 2, 3, 4, <strong>5</strong></p><p>Average <strong>3 ↑</strong></p><p class="mt-2">S: 6, 7, 8, 9</p><p>Average <strong>7.5 ↑</strong></p></div>
</div>
<div class="border-l-4 border-accent pl-4 text-base"><p><strong>Everyone together: average 5 both before and after.</strong></p><p>All nine numbers are unchanged.</p></div>
<figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">Five is below S’s original average of 7, so removing it raises that average. It is above R’s average of 2.5, so adding it raises R’s average too. The overall average stays the same because the group sizes change.</figcaption></figure>